declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"matchingSemantics","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"semanticLevel","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/RegexSemanticLevel","text":"RegexSemanticLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17_StringProcessing18RegexSemanticLevelV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Regex","preciseIdentifier":"s:17_StringProcessing5RegexV","text":"Regex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"RegexOutput","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17_StringProcessing5RegexV0C6Outputa"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"parameters":[{"name":"semanticLevel","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The semantics to use during matching."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The modified regular expression."}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When matching with grapheme cluster semantics (the default),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metacharacters like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\w"},{"type":"text","text":", custom character classes, and character"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"class instances like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".any"},{"type":"text","text":" match a grapheme cluster when possible,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corresponding with the default string representation. In addition,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matching with grapheme cluster semantics compares characters using their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"canonical representation, corresponding with how strings comparison works.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When matching with Unicode scalar semantics, metacharacters and character","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"classes always match a single Unicode scalar value, even if that scalar"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"comprises part of a grapheme cluster."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These semantic levels can lead to different results, especially when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"working with strings that have decomposed characters. In the following"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"queRegex"},{"type":"text","text":" matches any 3-character string that begins with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"q\""},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let composed = \"qué\"","let decomposed = \"que\\u{301}\"","","let queRegex = \/^q..$\/","","print(composed.contains(queRegex))","\/\/ Prints \"true\"","print(decomposed.contains(queRegex))","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When using Unicode scalar semantics, however, the regular expression only","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matches the composed version of the string, because each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"type":"text","text":" matches a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"single Unicode scalar value."}]},{"code":["let queRegexScalar = queRegex.matchingSemantics(.unicodeScalar)","print(composed.contains(queRegexScalar))","\/\/ Prints \"true\"","print(decomposed.contains(queRegexScalar))","\/\/ Prints \"false\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Regex\/matchingSemantics(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Regex/matchingSemantics(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/regex\/matchingsemantics(_:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a regular expression that matches with the specified semantic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Regex\/matchingSemantics(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"matchingSemantics","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17_StringProcessing18RegexSemanticLevelV","text":"RegexSemanticLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17_StringProcessing5RegexV","text":"Regex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17_StringProcessing5RegexV0C6Outputa","text":"RegexOutput","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"matchingSemantics(_:)"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/RegexSemanticLevel":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A semantic level to use during regex matching."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RegexSemanticLevel"}],"title":"RegexSemanticLevel","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RegexSemanticLevel"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/regexsemanticlevel","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/RegexSemanticLevel"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift","type":"topic","title":"Standard Library","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Standard Library","kind":"text"}],"ki